                <pb facs="0535" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6363 St 2/505</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chief of the Division of the American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bonsal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President of the
                        Standard Oil Company of New Jersey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Farish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-31">December 31, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Farish</hi>: Please accept my thanks for
                    your letter of December 16, 1940 enclosing a copy of a proposed formula for a
                    settlement of the difficulties between the Standard Oil Company of Bolivia and
                    the Bolivian Government. Your continued cooperation is greatly appreciated and
                    the suggested formula and your comments are being carefully studied in the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi> W. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
